3 Key Market Drivers
AI and High-Bandwidth Memory Demand: Expansion of AI servers, accelerators and high-bandwidth memory is increasing demand for advanced polished and epitaxial silicon wafers.
Growing 300 mm Wafer Adoption: Advanced logic and memory manufacturing increasingly relies on 300 mm wafers, supporting investment in high-capacity and high-quality wafer production.
Global Semiconductor Fab Expansion: New and expanded semiconductor fabrication facilities across North America, Europe and Asia are creating additional requirements for qualified wafer supply.

Vertical Industry Watch
The semiconductor industry remains the central demand engine for silicon wafers, with AI computing creating additional requirements for advanced logic and memory production. Automotive electronics, power management, MEMS, sensors and photonics are also broadening the application base. The transition toward advanced semiconductor nodes increases the importance of wafer purity, surface flatness, defect control, epitaxy and qualification. At the same time, geographic diversification of semiconductor manufacturing is creating opportunities for suppliers capable of supporting new fabs with qualified products, technical assistance and reliable logistics. Sustainability is also becoming increasingly important because silicon wafer production requires significant electricity, water and chemical inputs.

